title: '[pallet-revive] Deletion queue keeps the native deposit records of a re-created contract'

doc:
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    A contract can be created and terminated in one transaction and then created again at the
    same address in a later transaction, with `CREATE2` and the same deployer, code and salt.
    The new contract now keeps its per-payer native deposit records while the deletion queue
    is still removing the storage of the terminated contract, so freeing storage in the new
    contract refunds the native deposit to its payer. Before, the deletion queue cleared those
    records.

- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    No migration is needed.

    `ContractInfo::process_deletion_queue_batch` now clears the `NativeDepositOf` rows of a
    queued contract only while no contract is live at its address. The child trie of the
    terminated contract is removed as before.

    The per-entry deletion-queue weight (`WeightInfo::deletion_queue_per_entry`) now includes
    one `AccountInfoOf` read. Runtimes should regenerate their `pallet_revive` weights.

    `pallet-revive-fixtures` gains the `ClearableContributorStorage` and
    `ClearableContributorFactory` test contracts and their generated bindings. Existing
    fixtures are unchanged.

crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-revive-fixtures
  bump: minor
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
